---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import QuickMenu from '../components/QuickMenu.astro';
import { BUSINESS, hasReviewProof } from '../data/business';
import { attestedServices } from '../data/services';
import { ROUTED_TOWNS } from '../data/authorised';
import { COUNTY_NAMES } from '../data/geo';
import { linkableTowns } from '../lib/geo';
import { title, description } from '../lib/seo';
import { faqNode } from '../lib/schema';

const counties = [...new Set(ROUTED_TOWNS.map((c) => c.county))].map((c) => COUNTY_NAMES[c]);
const services = attestedServices();
const towns = linkableTowns();
const faqs = [
  { q: 'What areas do you cover?', a: `Blouin Pest Services works across ${counties.slice(0, -1).join(', ')} and ${counties.slice(-1)} in southern and central Maine.` },
  { q: 'Do you charge for an inspection?', a: 'No. Inspections and quotes are free, and the quote separates treatment from any sealing or exclusion work so you can see what you are paying for.' },
  { q: 'Who turns up?', a: `${BUSINESS.owner.name} does the inspection, the treatment and the follow-up. It is the same person each visit.` },
  { q: 'How soon can someone come out?', a: BUSINESS.emergency },
];
const t = title('Maine Pest Control');
const d = description('Owner-operated pest control across southern and central Maine: rodents, ants, ticks, mosquitoes, cockroaches and bed bugs. Free inspections. Call or text 207-740-4441.');
---
<BaseLayout title={t} description={d} path="/" extraNodes={[faqNode('/', faqs)]}>
  <h1>Pest control across Maine, from the person who does the work</h1>

  <div class="answer">
    <p>
      <strong>Blouin Pest Services is owner-operated.</strong> {BUSINESS.owner.name} inspects, treats and follows up —
      rodents, ants, ticks, mosquitoes, cockroaches and bed bugs — across {counties.slice(0, -1).join(', ')} and {counties.slice(-1)}.
      Inspections and quotes are free, and the quote separates the treatment from any sealing or repair work, so you can
      see what you are buying and compare it against anyone else's.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="cta-row">
    <a class="cta" href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phoneE164}`}>Call {BUSINESS.phone}</a>
    <a class="cta ghost" href={`sms:${BUSINESS.phoneE164}`}>Text {BUSINESS.phone}</a>
  </div>
  <p class="cta-note">{BUSINESS.hours} &middot; {BUSINESS.emergency}</p>

  <QuickMenu label="What we handle" items={services.map((s) => ({ href: `/services/${s.slug}/`, label: s.name }))} />
  <QuickMenu label="Where we work" items={towns.map((x) => ({ href: `/locations/${x.slug}/`, label: x.name }))} />

  {hasReviewProof() && (
    <p class="proof">
      <a href="/reviews/">Rated {BUSINESS.reviews.rating.toFixed(1)} from {BUSINESS.reviews.count} Google reviews</a> — read from the Google
      Business Profile on {BUSINESS.reviews.observed}. {BUSINESS.customers.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + BUSINESS.customers.slice(1)}.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>What we get called for most</h2>
  <p>
    Three jobs account for most of the calls, and each is a different kind of problem.
    <a href="/services/rodent-control/">Rodents</a> arrive with the first hard cold and are a sealing problem as much as
    a treatment one. <a href="/services/carpenter-ant-control/">Carpenter ants</a> show up in spring and are usually a
    moisture problem in timber a gutter or a window seal has been wetting. <a href="/services/tick-control/">Ticks</a>
    are a yard problem rather than a house problem, and the treatment follows the edge of the property rather than the
    building. The other ten are listed under <a href="/services/">services</a>, and the menu above jumps straight to any of them.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens when you call</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Inspect first.</strong> The room you noticed the problem in is usually not the room the problem lives in.</li>
    <li><strong>Treat what is there</strong>, in the licensed category the work falls under.</li>
    <li><strong>Close the way in.</strong> Sealing is what stops you paying for the same job every year.</li>
    <li><strong>Write it down.</strong> Every visit produces a record of what was found, what was applied and what is recommended — including work that belongs to another trade.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Exclusion, which is where we are most useful</h2>
  <p>
    Treatment kills what is inside the building today. Sealing decides whether you are making this call again next
    autumn. Most of the rodent work here ends with a list of gaps — a dryer vent, a sill plate, a gap behind a bulkhead —
    and the quote prices that separately so you can do it now or do it later with your eyes open.
  </p>

  <h2>Where we work</h2>
  <p>
    Southern and central Maine: {counties.join(', ')}. {BUSINESS.radius} Call and ask about your town — if it is outside
    the area we cover we will say so rather than booking it.
  </p>

  <h2>When we are busiest, and when we are not</h2>
  <p>
    Tick and mosquito programmes run monthly from April to September. Rodent work peaks with the first hard cold, and
    exclusion done in September prevents the winter that follows. If you are reading this outside tick season, that is the
    cheapest month of the year to have the building sealed properly.
  </p>

  <h2>Licensed, and checkable</h2>
  <p>
    {BUSINESS.license.type} #{BUSINESS.license.number}, categories {BUSINESS.license.categories.map((c) => c.split(' ')[0]).join(' and ')},
    licensed and regulated by the {BUSINESS.license.authority}. <a href="/compliance/maine-pesticide-licensing/">What that means and how to check it</a>.
  </p>

  <Faq faqs={faqs} />

  <CallToAction />
</BaseLayout>
